## 🔍 Security Best Practices

### 1. Minimum Privilege Principle ✅
- AWS credentials should only allow necessary operations
- Database credentials should use read-only if possible for logging endpoints

### 2. Rotational Keys ✅
- Implement secret rotation (AWS Secrets Manager handles this)
- Never use same credentials for development and production

### 3. Secret Lifecycle ✅
- Never commit `.env` files to version control
- Use `.env.example` as template (no actual values)
- Rotate secrets regularly (monthly for keys)

### 4. Access Control ✅
- Limit who can access the secret manager
- Use IAM policies to restrict access
- Enable MFA for secret access

### 5. Auditing ✅
- Enable CloudTrail for AWS Secrets Manager
- Log all secret accesses
- Monitor for unusual access patterns

### 6. Encryption at Rest ✅
- Secrets Manager stores encrypted secrets
- Never store keys in clear text
- Use database encryption (if using external database)

